<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Elizabeth Lucretia, Duchess of Teschen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1599–1653</span> · Also known as Elizabeth Lucretia of Cieszyn</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Elizabeth <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lucretia">Lucretia</a> was Duchess of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cieszyn">Cieszyn</a>, or Teschen, from 1625 to 1653, the last ruler of the Cieszyn branch of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piast-dynasty">Piast dynasty</a>. She succeeded her brother Frederick William and governed the duchy through the hardships of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-tyrants">the Thirty</a> Years' War. On her death the duchy passed to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburgs</a> as kings of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohemia">Bohemia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/elizabeth-lucretia-duchess-of-teschen.jpg" alt="Elizabeth Lucretia, Duchess of Teschen" width="320" height="348" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Eduardschnack · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Elisabeth_Lucretia_of_Teschen.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
